  "id": "withdrawal-design",
  "term": "withdrawal design",
  "definition": "A withdrawal design is a study approach that alternates periods when a program or intervention is given with periods when it is not given, often in an ABAB sequence. This pattern is used to compare changes across the on and off phases.",
